      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_44825efc",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image displays a group of diverse women posing together, juxtaposed with text claiming 'over 620 000 white people died to free black slaves' and 'so please lets cut the bullshit out - jf16'. The overall intent is hateful, as it attempts to delegitimize the historical and moral significance of the abolitionist movement by framing the sacrifice of white lives as a justification for contemporary racial dynamics. The text is a false and inflammatory claim that trivializes the immense suffering and loss of life during the American Civil War and the broader struggle for abolition. The meme uses the image of diverse women to visually contrast with the racially charged text, potentially implying that the historical sacrifice was made for the benefit of Black people, which is a distortion of history. The inclusion of the username 'jf16' suggests this is a user-generated meme intended to provoke or spread misinformation. The meme is harmful as it promotes a distorted historical narrative that can incite racial division and undermine the understanding of the abolitionist movement's true motivations and the moral imperative behind it. The intent is to provoke outrage or dismiss the historical context of slavery and abolition, which is a form of hate speech targeting Black people and their historical struggle for freedom.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_a57d3724"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
